          "english": "On a small fruit farm near the Straits of Malacca, Lim Kok Ann is down to just one tree growing kedondong, a crunchy, sour berry that Malaysians mostly use in pickles(腌菜) and salads. \"It's not very well-known,\" says the 45-year-old, who is instead focusing on longan(龙眼) berries and pineapples, which have bigger markets. \"We have to grow what is profitable,\" he says.",
