          "english": "Prof Azam-Ali explains that just four crops—wheat, maize, rice and soybean—provide two-thirds of the world's food supply. \"We're dependent on these four,\" he says. \"But actually there're 7,000 crops we've been farming for thousands of years. We ignore all of those.\" Researchers are trying to unlock the potential of these ignored crops—plants they describe as forgotten, under-used or \"alternative\" as they are displaced by increasingly uniform diets fuelled by processed ingredients from the major crops.",
          "chinese": "Azam-Ali 教授解释说，仅小麦、玉米、水稻和大豆这四种作物，就提供了世界粮食供应量的三分之二。“我们依赖这四种作物。”他说，“但实际上，我们已经耕种了7,000种作物数千年。我们却忽视了它们。”研究人员正努力挖掘这些被忽视作物的潜力。这些植物被他们称为被遗忘的、未充分利用的或“替代性”作物，因为随着以主要作物加工原料为基础的饮食日益趋同，它们逐渐被排挤。",
