          "number": 5,
          "letter": "E",
          "english": "Forgotten crops hold key answers. By investing in neglected local plants, countries can reduce their reliance on imported crops and their carbon-heavy supply chains. Bringing back the variety of crops humans once ate also boosts food security at a time warming climates threaten existing crops. On top of that forgotten crops are among the most climate-resilient(具有气候韧性的) and nutritious, argues Azam-Ali. His summary is plain: \"Dietary diversification is critical to the future of humanity.\"",
          "chinese": "被遗忘的作物蕴含着解决问题的关键答案。通过投资于被忽视的本地植物，各国可以减少对进口作物及其高碳供应链的依赖。让人类曾经食用的作物多样性重新回归，也能在变暖的气候威胁现有作物之际提升粮食安全。除此之外，Azam-Ali 认为，被遗忘的作物是最具气候韧性、营养最丰富的作物之一。他的总结十分明确：“饮食多样化对人类的未来至关重要。”",
